# Reports are produced against real machines. They are sanitized by
# construction, but "sanitized" is a property of the code working correctly,
# not a guarantee - so they never enter git regardless. Belt and braces.
reports/
*.json
*.log

# Local run state, if anyone ever runs the toolkit straight out of the repo.
state.json

# Third-party stress and diagnostic utilities. Most do not permit
# redistribution, they are large and freely re-downloadable, and vendor
# binaries do not belong in a repo. The README explaining the folder stays.
tools/*
!tools/README.md
